// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: Sudo Spawning a Shell With No Arguments
// Sigma ID: 590585fd-ea0b-4baa-b391-7d9a2d45d5ba
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-04-30 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1068, T1548.001
// Description: Detects sudo spawning a shell where the parent CommandLine ends with just "sudo" and carries no
//   subcommand or flags. Bare sudo has no legitimate code path that opens a shell — it only prints
//   usage. A shell child under these conditions indicates the process was hijacked, e.g. via
//   shellcode calling execve("/bin/sh", NULL) inside a poisoned SUID binary.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/
//   - https://xint.io/blog/copy-fail-linux-distributions
//   - https://github.com/theori-io/copy-fail-CVE-2026-31431
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/f978f702f404ad5049a7bbac0dd729a9959455fa/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_sudo_bare_shell_spawn.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/sudo" and InitiatingProcessCommandLine endswith "sudo" and (FolderPath endswith "/sh" or FolderPath endswith "/dash" or FolderPath endswith "/bash" or FolderPath endswith "/ksh" or FolderPath endswith "/zsh" or FolderPath endswith "/ash" or FolderPath endswith "/tcsh" or FolderPath endswith "/csh")
